ost trackers put the average near a tie.\n\nMoney is the sharpest asymmetry: Jackson has raised roughly $119 million to Bottoms' $6 million and holds a large cash-on-hand edge heading into the final stretch. Prediction markets price Bottoms modestly above even odds, and most race raters call it a tossup. Medicaid and data-center issues are driving the debate, and the outcome will likely hinge on turnout in metro Atlanta versus Republican gains elsewhere.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6414, "margin": 1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5561, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5612, "margin": 0.5}]}